# Accessibility (WCAG 2.2 AA)

## Structure
- `<html lang="en-GB">` on every page.
- One `<h1>` per page. Never skip heading levels.
- Use landmarks: `<header>`, `<nav>`, `<main id="main">`, `<footer>`.
- The first focusable element is a "Skip to content" link targeting `#main`.
- Links go somewhere, buttons do something. Never use a `<div>` with a click handler.

## Colour and contrast
- Body text 4.5:1 minimum. Large text (24px+, or 18.66px+ bold) and UI parts 3:1.
- Accent `#1C4AA6` on white = 8.15:1 and on surface `#F4F7FD` = 7.59:1, OK for text. On near-black it's about 2.1:1, so never use it for text on dark backgrounds.
- Never use colour alone to carry meaning (links in body copy are underlined).

## Focus and keyboard
- Every interactive element is reachable and usable by keyboard, in visual order.
- Visible focus with `:focus-visible`: 2px solid outline, 2px offset, 3:1 against its background. Never `outline: none` without a replacement.
- Touch targets at least 44×44px on mobile. Never below 24×24px (WCAG 2.5.8).

## Images and media
- Every `<img>` has `alt`. Decorative images get `alt=""`.
- Case-study images get alt text that states what the image shows and why it matters, not "screenshot of".
- Always set `width` and `height` (or aspect-ratio) so the layout doesn't shift.

## Motion
- Wrap all non-essential motion in `@media (prefers-reduced-motion: no-preference)`.
- Animate only `transform` and `opacity`. Nothing auto-plays.

## Layout
- No horizontal page scroll from 320px to 1280px.
- Body text max 70ch per line. Text must reflow at 200% zoom with nothing lost.
